question:
Suppose \(a\) and \(b\) are real numbers satisfying \(-3\leq a\leq1\) and \(-2\leq b\leq4\). If values of \(a\) and \(b\) are selected randomly, what is the probability that \(a\cdot b\) is positive? Give your answer as a common fraction.
A. \frac{5}{12}
B. \frac{5}{11}
C. \frac{7}{12}
D. \frac{5}{17}
